    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2017-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let the numbers be \\(x\\) and \\(y,\\) so \\(x+y=4xy.\\)\n\nDividing both sides by \\(xy\\) gives \\[ \\dfrac{x+y}{xy}=4, \\] and the left side is exactly \\(\\dfrac{1}{y}+\\dfrac{1}{x}.\\) So the sum of the reciprocals is \\(4.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "The sum of reciprocals is \\(\\dfrac{1}{x}+\\dfrac{1}{y}=\\dfrac{x+y}{xy}\\)",
        "Divide the equation \\(x+y=4xy\\) by \\(xy\\)"
      ],
